{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Korah took.</b> It is found in חלק: Reish Lakish said — he took a bad acquisition for himself. Korah — who made a bald spot [kerachah] in Israel. Another interpretation: Korah rises by gematria to שד״ד — that he acted violently [shaded] and did not keep the commandments of the Holy One, blessed be He." "<b>son of Yitzhar.</b> For he boiled the entire world like the afternoon heat [tzohorayim]." "<b>son of Kehat.</b> For he blinded [hikh'ah] the eyes of those who gave birth to him." "<b>son of Levi.</b> For he became an accompaniment [levayah] for Gehenna. And one asks: let him also be counted as 'son of Ya'akov' — a son who dragged [she'akev] himself to Gehenna. And the answer: Rabbi Shmuel bar Rav Yitzchak said — Ya'akov sought mercy for himself, as it is said: ״ובקהלם אל תחד כבודי״." "<b>and Datan.</b> Who transgressed the law [dat]." "<b>And Abiram.</b> Who lost himself from doing repentance." "<b>And On.</b> Who sat all his days in anguish." "<b>Ben Pelet.</b> A son for whom wonders were done." "<b>The sons of Reuben.</b> A son who saw and understood. Midrash — because Reuben was the firstborn, they said: we have a share in the priesthood. Therefore they too held fast to the dispute." "<b>And Rav says:</b> On ben Pelet — his wife saved him. She said to him: What difference does it make to you? If Moses is the great one, you are the disciple; if Korah is the great one, you are the disciple. He said to her: And what can I do, for I was with them in the counsel and I was sworn together with them? She said to him: I know that the entire congregation is holy, as it is said: ״כי כל העדה כלם קדושים״. Go sit in your house, and I will save you. She gave him wine to drink, intoxicated him, and laid him down inside the house. She sat at the doorway and uncovered her hair. Whoever came saw her and turned back. Meanwhile they were swallowed up, and he was saved and remained alive — ״בנפש״ חכמו״ נשים בנתה ביתה ואול״ בידיה תהרסנו״ — this is the wife of Korah, who strengthened her husband's hand in the dispute. And she said to him: See what Moses has done! He made himself king; he made his brother High Priest; he made his brother's sons deputy priests. If terumah comes, he says: let it be for the priest. First tithe as well — that which you give, he says: one part of ten shall be for the priest. And furthermore, he decreed upon you to shave yourselves, as it is said: ״והעבירו תער על כל בשרם״. And he moves you about like tied bundles, as it is said: ״והנפת אותם תנופה״. He said to her: He too does the same! She said to him: He, since he is the great one and his son-in-law, is as one who says 'let me die with the Philistines.' He said to you: make techelet! And if it were the case that techelet is important, take off a garment of techelet and clothe all the students of your school in it. And therefore the passage of tzitzit was juxtaposed here, to say to you: that through techelet the dispute was sustained. For at that time Korah made a feast for all those great men, and they all wrapped themselves in tallitot that were entirely techelet. Korah said to Moses: Are these tallitot exempt from techelet or not? He said to him: They are obligated. He said to him: Four threads of techelet exempt a tallit that is entirely techelet — is it not logical that it should exempt itself? He said to him: A house that is full of books — is it exempt from mezuzah or not? He said to him: It is obligated. He said to him: The entire Torah, all two hundred and seventy-five passages, do not exempt the house, but the two passages in the mezuzah exempt the house — you do not command us except from your own heart!"], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:45.325294640Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}